Phase 6 Task 6.2 (bead VieNeuTTSApp-nqx.8.2) — every synthesis surface offers
only what the ACTIVE engine profile can serve.

Delivered:
- New `components/EngineState.qml` singleton (registered in both qmldirs, the
  Theme precedent): the one place that answers the three capability questions
  a surface asks — which voices may this profile offer (voiceGroups:
  VieNeu's region-grouped catalog / a Qwen profile's pinned speakers or
  enrolled clones, never a mix), does its engine take a language
  (languageTakesParameter: an engine that ignores the argument gets no
  control, with the note saying so), and can it synthesize at all right now
  (readiness/statusText/blocked/blockerReason).
- VoicePicker: flatModel comes from EngineState.voiceGroups; `effectiveVoice`
  is the submission voice (picker choice, else the profile's own fallback —
  VieNeu's Settings default validated against the catalog, a Qwen profile's
  first offered voice); a profile with nothing to offer is disabled with the
  reason in its trigger (+ tooltip); `voiceInfoFor` lets a capability row
  carry its persona fields explicitly (a pinned speaker's native language
  rides in the region chip); group headers are no longer selectable rows.
- LanguagePicker: `takesLanguage` hides the combo for an engine that takes no
  language parameter, and the note explains why.
- TextTab / SynthesisBar + ParagraphTab / AudiobookTab / SubtitleCard: the
  language control, the submission voice (effectiveVoice) and the primary
  action gates (Generate, Ctrl+Return, Run all, chapter render, cue render,
  Render & play) all read that one derivation, so a disabled action carries
  the install/enrollment reason instead of failing on click.
- EngineProfilePicker now renders EngineState.readiness/statusText/deviceLabel:
  one derivation, so the readiness badge and a disabled Generate button can
  never disagree.

